**Definition 3.4 (body codecs).** The S-body and B-body are the strictly
lexicographically ordered lists of their paths, empty root path included
in S. The T-body is a list of patch records. A record has, in order, native
row/version/phase and defined input/read/output labels, reached old
operand identities, the ordered probes/results, target assignments,
new-template roles and commitment/receipt label. Undefined labels use an
explicit absent tag. Each sublist uses PVC.2 and fixed arity records.
Identities are the port/creation position and the fixed constructor role,
with root/scaffold roles separately tagged. Repeated operations remain
repeated list items. There is no endpoint snapshot in this body.

The M-body is the eight-tagged-list serialization of Definition 4.2. Raw
eight-bit cell records use original track order. All list orders and
record arities are fixed there. Serializing a right is serializing its
represented value; it issues no live TOK.

